WEBVTT

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:40.290
So I says, "Supercollider?
I just met her."

00:00:42.543 --> 00:00:45.045
And then they built the supercollider.

00:00:45.128 --> 00:00:47.631
Thank you. You've been a great audience.

00:00:49.716 --> 00:00:52.177
Humorbot 5.0, ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:52.261 --> 00:00:56.181
Our next stand-up's a veteran
of four comedy traffic schools.

00:00:56.265 --> 00:00:59.810
Give it way up for Bobcat Zoidberg!

00:00:59.893 --> 00:01:01.770
All right!

00:01:04.439 --> 00:01:06.859
Earth. What a planet.

00:01:06.942 --> 00:01:09.736
On Earth, you enjoy eating a tasty clam.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:13.657
On my planet,
clams enjoy eating a tasty you.

00:01:15.325 --> 00:01:17.661
Maybe I'm not yelling loud enough.

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:21.123
On Earth, everybody is always
looking for a giant squid.

00:01:21.206 --> 00:01:22.374
On my planet...

00:01:25.169 --> 00:01:26.420
Reload.

00:01:27.588 --> 00:01:31.216
So these three parasitic worms
bore into a human's head...

00:01:33.051 --> 00:01:35.220
...and they walk up to the bar
and then...

00:01:35.345 --> 00:01:38.015
Uh-oh. Wait! Stop! I've got more!

00:01:44.438 --> 00:01:48.734
My whole life I worked on that act,
and they hated it.

00:01:48.817 --> 00:01:51.361
You're a crazy, penniless lobster doctor.

00:01:51.445 --> 00:01:53.405
No combination of you
should be a comedian.

00:01:53.488 --> 00:01:55.699
But comedy is in my valves.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:58.410
My Uncle Harold was a big Hollywood star

00:01:58.493 --> 00:02:00.704
back in the era of silent holograms.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.207
Your uncle was Harold Zoid?

00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:05.375
This I cannot deny.

00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:10.172
Why, I've been a Harold Zoid fan
since back when my hips were made of bone.

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:14.176
As it happens, I still have
some of my original 78s.

00:03:12.442 --> 00:03:13.443
You're right, crabby.

00:03:13.527 --> 00:03:15.696
He's a hell of a lot funnier
than you could ever be.

00:03:15.779 --> 00:03:17.990
Maybe so, but perhaps if I wrote him

00:03:18.073 --> 00:03:20.909
and asked for a few hundred pointers...

00:03:21.952 --> 00:03:24.705
This letter has to be very personal,

00:03:24.788 --> 00:03:26.665
so I'm writing it in my own ink.

00:03:31.461 --> 00:03:35.424
Dear Uncle Zoid, greetings
from your long-lost nephew.

00:03:35.507 --> 00:03:38.385
Norm and Sam and Sadie's boy?
Remember?

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:42.973
Now I am the most important doctor
at the delivery company where I work.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.642
But sadly,
my life is bereft of laughter.

00:03:46.268 --> 00:03:50.731
"I beg of you, Mr. Funny Uncle.
Teach me the comedy business.

00:03:50.814 --> 00:03:52.983
"Sincerely, Zoidberg."

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:55.194
Oh, isn't that nice he took the time?

00:03:55.277 --> 00:03:57.863
What's that scribble-di-gook?

00:03:57.946 --> 00:04:01.074
This is a fan letter
from my rich doctor nephew,

00:04:01.158 --> 00:04:04.995
who just might be my ticket
out of this flophouse, he might.

00:04:09.458 --> 00:04:11.084
Yeah, you'd better run.

00:04:18.175 --> 00:04:22.137
Dear rich doctor nephew,
I can help you be funny.

00:04:22.221 --> 00:04:25.557
The first funny thing you must do
is put all your money

00:04:25.641 --> 00:04:28.894
in the form of a cashier's check
and come to Hollywood.

00:04:28.977 --> 00:04:33.190
"Sincerely, Harold Zoid.
P.S. Cashier's check."

00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:36.652
Did you hear that?
I'm going to Hollywood!

00:04:53.502 --> 00:04:56.755
Welcome to Hollywood.
I must warn you,

00:04:56.839 --> 00:05:00.759
there's no refund if you get discovered
and leave the tour.

00:05:02.177 --> 00:05:04.888
I'm just kidding.
That never happens.

00:05:04.972 --> 00:05:09.726
Now, to your right,
you'll see 30th Century Fox studios.

00:05:09.810 --> 00:05:12.396
Fox uses those searchlights
to blind pilots,

00:05:12.479 --> 00:05:15.065
then film the resulting plane crashes.

00:05:18.902 --> 00:05:20.445
Neat.

00:05:20.529 --> 00:05:23.740
Ahead, you'll see the home of Mel Gibson,

00:05:23.866 --> 00:05:26.410
star of the hit film Bravehead.

00:05:28.078 --> 00:05:30.789
And do we have any fans of Calculon,

00:05:30.873 --> 00:05:33.584
star of the robot soap opera
All My Circuits?

00:05:33.792 --> 00:05:35.961
Oh! I am! Me! Bender is!

00:05:36.044 --> 00:05:40.591
Then you'll wanna get a close look
at his luxurious Bel Air home.

00:05:40.674 --> 00:05:42.384
Yes, I will. Yep!

00:05:47.472 --> 00:05:50.017
- Are you my new hot water heater?
- No, I'm Bender.

00:05:50.100 --> 00:05:52.644
- We met once. Remember?
- Absolutely not.

00:05:52.728 --> 00:05:55.522
Come on. Don't you remember
how much I was bugging you?

00:05:55.606 --> 00:05:56.690
'Cause it was a lot.

00:05:56.773 --> 00:06:00.444
- You remember, right?
- Look, I'm programmed to be very busy.

00:06:00.527 --> 00:06:04.072
Unless you can heat water to 212 degrees,
I'm not interested.

00:06:07.242 --> 00:06:09.328
Have you got
an extra "goto 10" line?

00:06:09.411 --> 00:06:11.205
I said I don't need a Bender.

00:06:11.288 --> 00:06:14.458
Bender? That was the other guy.
My name's Boiler.

00:06:16.877 --> 00:06:17.920
Nice work, Boiler.

00:06:18.003 --> 00:06:19.963
Thanks. And call me Bender.

00:06:24.218 --> 00:06:26.720
That's where I'm meeting Uncle Zoid
for lunch

00:06:26.803 --> 00:06:28.430
to discuss my Hollywood dreams.

00:06:28.514 --> 00:06:31.808
Next time you see me,
don't be surprised if I've eaten.

00:06:38.941 --> 00:06:42.402
Uncle Zoid, you're looking young enough
to be thrown back.

00:06:42.486 --> 00:06:45.072
Rich nephew! Come over here

00:06:45.155 --> 00:06:49.117
and give your uncle
a nice, big meal.

00:06:52.287 --> 00:06:56.124
So, here we are,
a still-famous film comedian...

00:06:56.208 --> 00:07:00.337
And a rich, respected doctor
with many surviving patients.

00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:04.007
Eating real food in a restaurant,
as we both often do.

00:07:04.091 --> 00:07:06.760
So, you want to be a comedian, is it?

00:07:06.844 --> 00:07:08.387
It's my lifelong dream.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:12.599
Well, that dream dies now!
You're unfunny and untalented!

00:07:12.683 --> 00:07:14.643
That's why you're perfect for drama.

00:07:15.018 --> 00:07:17.187
Hmm... Serious drama.

00:07:17.271 --> 00:07:20.065
Perhaps it is time
to give up comedy.

00:07:22.985 --> 00:07:27.364
I'm putting together a big drama picture
right now as we speak.

00:07:27.447 --> 00:07:31.702
The script is dynamite.
I know, because I wrote it myself.

00:07:31.827 --> 00:07:33.996
And with me directing and starring,

00:07:34.079 --> 00:07:37.875
I'll be back on top
after 50 miserable years...

00:07:38.792 --> 00:07:40.127
of fame.

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:42.796
Ah, fame. Where do I come in?

00:07:42.880 --> 00:07:46.258
This fame film has a juicy part for you

00:07:46.341 --> 00:07:49.970
if you completely finance it
with your doctor money.

00:07:50.053 --> 00:07:51.180
So, are you in?

00:07:51.805 --> 00:07:53.932
Uh... Okay.

00:07:54.016 --> 00:07:55.809
How much do I have to invest?

00:07:55.893 --> 00:07:58.478
Oh, not much. Not much. A million dollars.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:03.442
Then it's settled.
Another blockbuster Hollywood deal.

00:08:03.525 --> 00:08:04.902
What can I get you gentlemen?

00:08:04.985 --> 00:08:06.445
Is bread free?

00:08:06.528 --> 00:08:08.447
- Yeah.
- We'll split an order.

00:08:19.124 --> 00:08:20.501
What's with Monstro?

00:08:20.584 --> 00:08:23.629
He promised he'd give his Uncle Zoid
a million bucks to make a movie.

00:08:23.712 --> 00:08:27.674
I've only been here a day,
and already I'm a Hollywood phony.

00:08:27.758 --> 00:08:31.345
Perhaps I could call on
TV's Calculon to help,

00:08:31.428 --> 00:08:33.180
now that I'm in showbiz.

00:08:33.263 --> 00:08:37.100
- Since when have you been in the biz?
- Long enough, little man.

00:08:37.184 --> 00:08:38.769
Long enough.

00:08:57.037 --> 00:09:00.666
Calculon, as your hot water heater,
I would be remiss

00:09:00.749 --> 00:09:04.795
if I didn't bring you scripts that could
make you an international film star.

00:09:04.878 --> 00:09:06.797
Of course. Tell me about the project.

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:08.090
It's a movie.

00:09:08.173 --> 00:09:10.342
Interesting. Tell me more.

00:09:10.425 --> 00:09:11.677
Get this.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:16.431
For a scant one-million-dollar investment,
you can be the star.

00:09:16.515 --> 00:09:17.850
And?

00:09:17.933 --> 00:09:20.686
And, I guarantee it'll win you an Oscar.

00:09:20.769 --> 00:09:22.271
An Oscar, you say?

00:09:22.354 --> 00:09:26.066
That would get me out of this
festering rat's nest called television

00:09:26.149 --> 00:09:27.484
once and for all.

00:09:27.568 --> 00:09:29.194
Let me see the script.

00:09:30.279 --> 00:09:33.198
No. No, I don't like the font. Wait!

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:34.867
Harold Zoid?

00:09:35.158 --> 00:09:37.536
Was this written by the Harold Zoid?

00:09:37.619 --> 00:09:39.371
Written and xeroxed.

00:09:39.454 --> 00:09:40.539
Good heavens.

00:09:40.622 --> 00:09:43.709
A chance to work
with the legendary Harold Zoid.

00:09:43.792 --> 00:09:45.752
He's one of my great idols.

00:09:45.836 --> 00:09:48.255
And you say you can
guarantee me the Oscar?

00:09:48.338 --> 00:09:50.299
I can guarantee you anything you want.

00:09:50.382 --> 00:09:52.384
- Then I'll do it!
- Hooray!

00:09:52.634 --> 00:09:54.136
Here's your checkbook.

00:09:59.558 --> 00:10:00.684
Ladies and gentlemen,

00:10:00.767 --> 00:10:04.980
I give you our director,
the legendary Harold Zoid.

00:10:07.274 --> 00:10:10.819
Thank you.
A more classic movie plot there isn't.

00:10:10.903 --> 00:10:14.865
A son who does not want to follow
in his father's business,

00:10:14.948 --> 00:10:18.577
and that business
is being president of Earth no less.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.455
The son, as it happens,
is vice president.

00:10:21.538 --> 00:10:24.249
That plot makes perfect sense,
wink, wink.

00:10:24.333 --> 00:10:26.460
Bender, you said "wink, wink" out loud.

00:10:26.543 --> 00:10:28.212
No, I didn't. Raise middle finger.

00:10:30.881 --> 00:10:33.967
Now, remember,
and I can't stress this enough,

00:10:34.051 --> 00:10:35.260
this is a talkie,

00:10:35.344 --> 00:10:41.099
so I want the full gamut of emotions
from every actor in every scene.

00:10:41.183 --> 00:10:44.436
The Magnificent Three.
Scene one, take one.

00:10:44.520 --> 00:10:46.230
And action!

00:10:46.313 --> 00:10:49.399
Take back your gilded pen, Father.

00:10:49.483 --> 00:10:53.445
Signing bills into law
was always your dream, not mine.

00:10:53.529 --> 00:10:54.988
Cut! Cut! Cut it!

00:10:55.155 --> 00:10:59.743
I said this is a talkie, damn it!
You've got to emote more!

00:10:59.826 --> 00:11:02.663
And you extras.
Wave your arms and make faces.

00:11:02.746 --> 00:11:04.164
What is this? A morgue?

00:11:04.248 --> 00:11:08.085
The Magnificent Three.
Scene 10, take 95.

00:11:08.168 --> 00:11:11.171
Action! And I mean
circus-grade action.

00:11:11.255 --> 00:11:16.218
Sir, I call upon you
not as a president,

00:11:16.301 --> 00:11:18.595
but as a father!

00:11:21.557 --> 00:11:23.392
Cut! Cut! Cut it!

00:11:23.475 --> 00:11:25.853
Would you show a little emotion?

00:11:25.936 --> 00:11:29.690
People, people, please.
Just because it's a dramatic scene

00:11:29.773 --> 00:11:32.693
doesn't mean you can't
do a little comedy in the background.

00:11:32.776 --> 00:11:34.987
Throw a pie or two,
for God's sake.

00:11:42.494 --> 00:11:44.663
No!

00:11:50.919 --> 00:11:53.630
Cut! Cut it! Yuck!

00:11:53.714 --> 00:11:56.508
Look. It's all right, kid.
We'll get it in editing.

00:11:56.592 --> 00:11:58.552
All right. That's a wrap, everybody.

00:11:58.635 --> 00:12:01.597
I'm gonna see you all at the premiere,
which, by the way, when is?

00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:04.892
Well, editing is a long
and expensive process,

00:12:04.975 --> 00:12:08.937
but we spent all the money on pies,
so it'll be ready Friday.

00:12:16.653 --> 00:12:18.155
Nice turnout, Calculon.

00:12:18.238 --> 00:12:20.657
That Oscar is practically on your mantle.

00:12:20.741 --> 00:12:23.702
I just pray they like me
half as much as I do.

00:12:33.629 --> 00:12:39.218
I agreed to be your vice president,
but I never agreed to be your son.

00:12:43.430 --> 00:12:44.681
Thank you, Lieutenant Smith.

00:12:44.765 --> 00:12:47.059
Good morning,

00:12:47.142 --> 00:12:49.978
Mr. Vice President.

00:12:52.856 --> 00:12:54.691
Leela, we're missing the premiere.

00:12:54.775 --> 00:12:57.653
My only goal in life
is to attend a Hollywood shindig.

00:12:57.736 --> 00:12:59.613
Just pay the valet the two bucks.

00:12:59.696 --> 00:13:01.907
No. It's the principle of the thing.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:04.618
Besides, I think I see a parking lot
up ahead.

00:13:14.086 --> 00:13:17.714
Father, I have asked you
to join meon the White House roof

00:13:17.798 --> 00:13:20.717
so we could have
a heart-to-heart talk.

00:13:20.801 --> 00:13:23.762
I will never follow
in your footsteps.

00:13:23.846 --> 00:13:27.266
Here is my resignation
as vice president.

00:13:27.349 --> 00:13:31.520
No! My son will not
shame me like this.

00:13:31.603 --> 00:13:34.231
I would sooner die,
I would.

00:13:34.314 --> 00:13:35.691
Father! The ledge!

00:13:37.776 --> 00:13:38.777
Oh...

00:13:39.778 --> 00:13:41.947
The president is dead.

00:13:42.030 --> 00:13:44.825
Congratulations, Mr. President.

00:13:44.908 --> 00:13:50.038
No!

00:13:52.958 --> 00:13:55.460
Woo-hoo! Yeah! He's a visionary!

00:13:56.587 --> 00:13:59.173
Everyone walked out. They hated it.

00:13:59.256 --> 00:14:01.842
I've seen plagues that had
better opening nights than this.

00:14:01.925 --> 00:14:05.012
You said that Oscar was practically
on my mantle.

00:14:05.095 --> 00:14:08.056
Now you know why I used the qualifier
"practically."

00:14:08.140 --> 00:14:11.685
You listen to me.
I'm out a million bucks here.

00:14:11.768 --> 00:14:16.398
You get me that Oscar or you're dead,
you and these sniveling lobsters!

00:14:16.481 --> 00:14:18.734
Dead! You hear me? Dead!

00:14:20.527 --> 00:14:22.696
Oy! Now he emotes!

00:14:30.579 --> 00:14:35.083
400 categories,
and not a single nomination for me.

00:14:35.167 --> 00:14:37.169
But you won this Golden Globe.

00:14:37.252 --> 00:14:39.713
Piffle! That's the Emmy of movie awards!

00:14:40.881 --> 00:14:42.591
I told you I want an Oscar!

00:14:42.674 --> 00:14:44.676
Then maybe you should act better.

00:14:44.760 --> 00:14:46.595
The Oscar isn't about acting,

00:14:46.678 --> 00:14:51.016
it's about earning the respect
and admiration of the creative community.

00:14:51.099 --> 00:14:52.601
How about we rig the awards?

00:14:52.684 --> 00:14:53.977
That's fine too.

00:14:58.982 --> 00:15:02.986
It's no use. The tar is too thick.
Plus, I think I flooded it.

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:05.405
Well, we missed the premiere,
and we're gonna die.

00:15:05.489 --> 00:15:07.991
Might as well enjoy the sights.

00:15:08.075 --> 00:15:11.286
Oh, my God. Sylvester Stallone!

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:14.665
This is where you live?

00:15:14.748 --> 00:15:17.709
I thought you were
a big-shot Hollywood movie star.

00:15:17.793 --> 00:15:21.129
No, I'm not.
I am an even bigger liar than you.

00:15:21.213 --> 00:15:25.259
My career went down the tubes
the day they invented Smell-A-Vision.

00:15:25.342 --> 00:15:27.553
Calculon's gonna kill us for sure,

00:15:27.636 --> 00:15:29.721
and it's all everybody else's fault.

00:15:29.805 --> 00:15:35.477
All I wanted was for people
to think of me one last time before I die.

00:15:35.561 --> 00:15:40.357
What are you talking about, Uncle?
Everybody remembers Harold Zoid.

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:43.193
As a pathetic has-been,
they remember me.

00:15:43.277 --> 00:15:48.156
- As a forgotten relic, they remember me.
- It's better to die now.

00:15:48.240 --> 00:15:52.452
No! This is one death
Dr. Zoidberg won't be responsible for.

00:15:52.536 --> 00:15:54.079
Zoidberg away!

00:16:04.423 --> 00:16:09.094
Hi. I'm Joan Rivers's head.
I tell you, I've had so many face-lifts,

00:16:09.178 --> 00:16:11.972
they finally lifted it
right off my body.

00:16:12.055 --> 00:16:13.557
It's true! It's true!

00:16:13.682 --> 00:16:18.520
Oh, oh, oh! Here comes Jack Nicholson's
DNA reconstituted in a gorilla body.

00:16:22.566 --> 00:16:23.942
Catering.

00:16:25.652 --> 00:16:26.778
Oh. Ugh...

00:16:29.656 --> 00:16:33.744
Oh! And here's washed-up actor
what's-his-name, Harold Zoid.

00:16:33.827 --> 00:16:37.456
Are you presenting one of those
tacky honorary awards or just getting one?

00:16:37.539 --> 00:16:39.458
I'm a seat filler, Joan's head.

00:16:39.541 --> 00:16:43.003
My only marketable skill
is to occupy space.

00:16:47.424 --> 00:16:50.385
You know, the second I don't win
that award,

00:16:50.469 --> 00:16:51.720
you're cat food.

00:16:51.803 --> 00:16:53.055
Right, Boxy?

00:16:59.186 --> 00:17:03.857
And now, the host
of the 1,074th Academy Awards,

00:17:03.941 --> 00:17:07.152
Billy Crystal!

00:17:07.236 --> 00:17:09.488
Now I know how a PEZ dispenser feels.

00:17:11.990 --> 00:17:13.575
Oh, you like that one, Jack?

00:17:18.455 --> 00:17:20.666
All right. We're already one hour behind.

00:17:21.834 --> 00:17:23.126
Our first award tonight,

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:26.004
best cinematography
in a non-visible spectrum.

00:17:28.131 --> 00:17:29.508
It's been two weeks.

00:17:29.591 --> 00:17:32.344
You wanna play tic-tac-toe again
before we eat our shoes?

00:17:32.427 --> 00:17:35.806
No. I always knew
I'd die at the bottom of a pit.

00:17:35.889 --> 00:17:37.391
But a pit full of tar?

00:17:38.892 --> 00:17:43.105
What was that?
A tar dolphin or a tar shark?

00:17:43.188 --> 00:17:46.775
It's some kind of hollow tube
devoid of human life.

00:17:46.859 --> 00:17:51.321
The Los Angeles subway!
We can blast our way in and escape!

00:17:51.405 --> 00:17:53.949
All right, but I still feel like
having a shoe.

00:17:58.829 --> 00:18:00.497
What category are they on?

00:18:00.581 --> 00:18:02.916
They're giving out
the minor technical awards.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.376
I think they're up to writing.

00:18:04.459 --> 00:18:06.795
That just leaves
best soft drink product placement

00:18:06.879 --> 00:18:07.921
and then best actor.

00:18:08.005 --> 00:18:09.173
We don't have much time.

00:18:09.381 --> 00:18:13.010
And the nominees for
best soft drink product placement are...

00:18:13.093 --> 00:18:15.596
The Pepsi Generation.

00:18:15.679 --> 00:18:17.848
They Call Me Mr. Pibb.

00:18:17.931 --> 00:18:20.350
And Snow White
and the 7 UPs.

00:18:22.561 --> 00:18:26.356
And now, to present the award
for best actor,

00:18:26.690 --> 00:18:32.571
a bit player in the flop movie,
The Magnificent Three, Dr. Zoidberg!

00:18:37.075 --> 00:18:40.078
Okay, Boxy.
Keep your prong on the trigger.

00:18:41.246 --> 00:18:44.124
And the nominees
for best actor are...

00:18:44.208 --> 00:18:48.253
Sir Laurence
in The Merchant of Venus.

00:18:48.337 --> 00:18:52.508
Hive Mind Gamma 7-X
in Bikini Party Summer.

00:18:52.591 --> 00:18:56.094
The Soda Machine Robot
in Bikini Party Summer.

00:18:56.178 --> 00:18:59.890
Mark Jones
in How Beige Was My Jacket.

00:18:59.973 --> 00:19:02.309
And instead of the fifth guy,

00:19:02.392 --> 00:19:06.897
Calculon, for his powerhouse performance
in The Magnificent Three.

00:19:09.233 --> 00:19:10.901
Uh-oh. He read the wrong name.

00:19:10.984 --> 00:19:13.403
Shh! Just play along like they did
for Marisa Tomei.

00:19:13.487 --> 00:19:17.699
Hooray! I won't be murdered!
I'll live another day.

00:19:17.783 --> 00:19:23.080
Another day of pathetic, forgotten misery.

00:19:28.168 --> 00:19:29.503
And the winner is...

00:19:34.925 --> 00:19:38.637
And the winner,
instead of any of the nominees,

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:42.140
is the legendary Harold Zoid!

00:19:44.726 --> 00:19:46.311
What?

00:19:52.985 --> 00:19:55.279
Thank you. Thank you so much.

00:19:55.362 --> 00:19:57.489
You know, through all my ups and downs,

00:19:57.573 --> 00:20:00.534
I always thought
the most important thing in life

00:20:00.617 --> 00:20:02.286
was to win an Oscar.

00:20:02.369 --> 00:20:05.497
But tonight I realize
what's really important

00:20:05.581 --> 00:20:07.374
is to win two Oscars!

00:20:09.293 --> 00:20:11.128
I'm kidding. I'm kidding.

00:20:11.211 --> 00:20:15.132
What really matters in life
is that people care about you,

00:20:15.215 --> 00:20:18.135
whether it's a whole crowd...

00:20:18.218 --> 00:20:21.013
...or just one diehard fan.

00:20:22.306 --> 00:20:23.682
Aw!

00:20:33.108 --> 00:20:35.277
Thank you, nephew.

00:20:35.611 --> 00:20:37.237
Now I can die happy,

00:20:37.321 --> 00:20:40.199
10 seconds from now
when Calculon kills us.

00:20:43.535 --> 00:20:44.536
Harold Zoid!

00:20:44.620 --> 00:20:46.246
Hit the deck!

00:20:46.330 --> 00:20:47.831
Where's that Oscar?

00:20:47.915 --> 00:20:50.667
Here. Enjoy. What are you getting upset?

00:20:50.751 --> 00:20:53.462
It's slightly less fraudulent
for you to have it.

00:20:53.545 --> 00:20:56.840
Yes. Yes, it's a real beauty.

00:20:57.716 --> 00:21:00.219
Someday I hope
to win one of my own.

00:21:01.428 --> 00:21:03.931
Then you're not gonna kill us,
Your Majesty?

00:21:04.014 --> 00:21:07.559
Nay. I respect and admire Harold Zoid
too much

00:21:07.643 --> 00:21:09.603
to beat him to death with his own Oscar.

00:21:12.105 --> 00:21:13.440
Earthquake!

00:21:13.524 --> 00:21:15.108
Hit the deck!

00:21:15.192 --> 00:21:20.697
Let the Earth quake,
I've got somebody's Oscar!

00:21:28.372 --> 00:21:31.041
We made it!
I'm at a Hollywood party.

00:21:31.124 --> 00:21:33.252
I'm sorry, sir. This is a private...

00:21:33.335 --> 00:21:35.796
Oh, pardon me.
I see you're with Mr. Stallone.